  "worked_solution": "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $7$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n7=\\frac{7}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{7}{8}$ is $\\frac{8}{7}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n7÷\\frac{7}{8}=\\frac{7}{1}÷\\frac{7}{8}=\\frac{7}{1}\\times \\frac{8}{7}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{1}\\times \\frac{8}{7}=\\frac{7\\times 8}{1\\times 7}=\\frac{56}{7}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n56÷7=8\n$$",
